If a monster doesn't know where you are, there's a 1/4 chance it figures
it out, and won't forget until you move.

Otherwise, the assignment of where the monster thinks you _are_ is a bit
complicated, but ordinarily it picks a random square in a 5x5 grid,
centred on you, to which the monster could move (not a wall, etc), which
can be seen from your square.

Hence the effect of displacement is difficult to quantify - it depends on
the amount of open space around you, because the proportion of the
elegible spaces that are the space you are actually in is higher in open
areas, and also on the degree to which you move around.
